//RS //! D-QUERY-RETAIN1=A: one typed `Query<T>` surface over ordinary lists,
//RS //! checked readers, and checked SQL. Query plans and grouped reductions stay
//RS //! in this per-interpreter state; materialized results are ordinary lists.
//RS //! `DataStream<T>` remains one-shot and fallible, while typed loaders preserve
//RS //! ownership, authority, and snapshot state.
//RS //!
//RS //! `csv<T>`/`json<T>` use the call-site type argument at runtime; query
//RS //! callbacks use the same closure path as `list.map`/`.filter`/`.sort_by`.
//RS //! The shared query kernel is also used by the AOT and JIT tiers.
//RS //! parity: guard tests/dataflow_stream.rs::rolling_mean_nonfinite_matches_aot_and_default_dev
//RS //!
//RS //! Legacy carrier wrappers are intentionally absent.
//RS //! 
//RS //! 
